# ── OS / editor ──
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ── Node (if a static-site toolchain is added later) ──
node_modules/
dist/

# ── Generated example artifacts (regenerate from *.yaml + resource/script/ via the engine) ──
examples/**/out/
examples/**/out_*/
examples/**/video/
examples/**/.capture/
examples/**/*.mp4
examples/**/animation.html

# Narration mp3s are ignored EXCEPT under `resource/audio/`, which is committed so a
# clone can render an example without paying a TTS provider for recordings that already
# exist. The directory must be re-included before the files — git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
examples/**/*.mp3
!examples/*/resource/audio/
!examples/*/resource/audio/**

# ── Local authoring tools and scratch, not published ──
# Generators that produced a committed SVG (make_*.py / make_*.sh) and their input data
# are local work: useful to whoever ran them, noise to everyone cloning the examples.
# An example renders from what IS published — the committed scene SVGs and assets — so a
# clone never needs these to run.
#
#   resource/helper/  the stable authoring tools: generators, checks, rasterisers. Kept
#                     indefinitely; they are what you re-run after changing an input.
#   resource/temp/    genuinely temporary: logs, captures, intermediates. Deletable.
examples/**/*.py
examples/**/*.sh
examples/**/*.geojson
examples/**/resource/helper/
examples/**/resource/temp/

# Licensed stock audio lives at `resource/audio/source/` and stays UNPUBLISHED. It is an
# input rather than a build output — a clone cannot regenerate it the way it regenerates
# TTS narration — but stock-audio licences commonly forbid redistributing the file itself
# in substantially its original form, which is exactly what committing it would be.
# Each example's README names the track and where to fetch it instead.
#
# ⚠️ This re-exclusion must come AFTER the `resource/audio/` negation above, or the
# negation would publish it. An example that ships audio it genuinely owns can override
# this with a per-file negation once that right is established.
examples/*/resource/audio/source/

# ── Generated documentation-video artifacts ──────────────────────────────────
# `docs/video/src/` holds the SOURCES for the videos on the documentation site:
# the YAML, the SVG scenes, the narration scripts, and the narration audio.
#
# ⚠️ The narration mp3s here are TRACKED, unlike the ones under `examples/`.
# A reader cloning this repo can then render a documentation video without
# paying a TTS provider for audio that is already written and already recorded.
# That is the whole point of committing them, so do NOT add an `*.mp3` rule.
docs/video/**/out/
docs/video/**/.capture/
docs/video/**/animation.html
docs/video/**/*.mp4

# ── Working scratch — source-art variants, editor projects, intermediate exports ──
# Anything an example actually needs is archived INTO that example, never referenced
# out of here (the hiking-trails trace lives at resources/diagram/hiking_trace.png
# for exactly this reason).
examples/temp/
*.zip

# ── "thank you" example pieces — kept local, not published ──
examples/**/thank_you*

# ── AI-assistant config — local tooling, not published ──
.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/GEMINI.md

# Experimental diagram assets — kept local, not tracked
examples/microservices-flow/resources/diagram/grainy_background.svg
